---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

/**
 * PLACEHOLDER PRICING.
 *
 * Pricing and service definition are both recorded as BLOCKED in STATE.md:
 * there is no rate card, no retainer structure, and no measured delivery
 * hours per engagement to derive one from. The tiers below carry structure
 * and scope only — every figure is deliberately left as "On application"
 * rather than invented. Fill in from a real rate card before launch.
 */
const tiers = [
  {
    name: 'Answer Surface Audit',
    price: null,
    summary:
      'A one-off diagnosis. Where you stand in AI answers today, against a named competitor set, and what is causing it.',
    includes: [
      'Buying-intent prompt set, defined with you',
      'Run across ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini and Perplexity',
      'Brands named and in what order, per prompt, per engine',
      'The sources each answer was built from',
      'Entity check — whether models can resolve who you are',
      'A prioritised list of what would move the position',
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'Sprint',
    price: null,
    summary:
      'Fixed scope, fixed length. The audit, then the highest-leverage fixes executed, then a re-measure against the same prompt set.',
    includes: [
      'Everything in the audit',
      'Entity and structured-data corrections',
      'Answer-shaped content for the prompts that matter',
      'Third-party placement plan',
      'Re-measure on the frozen prompt set, with a control group',
    ],
  },
  {
    name: 'Retainer',
    price: null,
    summary:
      'Ongoing. Tracked position, continuous placement and content work, and reporting that separates our impact from everything else moving.',
    includes: [
      'Continuous tracking on a fixed prompt set',
      'Control prompts, deliberately unoptimised, to isolate causation',
      'Monthly reporting with raw metrics, not just a score',
      'Placement and content execution',
      'Quarterly review against the baseline',
    ],
  },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Service"
  description="What Brandure does: an answer surface audit, a fixed-scope sprint, or an ongoing retainer. Measurement first, then the work that moves the position."
>
  <h1>Service</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    Every engagement starts with a measurement, because without a baseline
    there is no way to show that anything we did afterwards worked.
  </p>

  <h2>How the work runs</h2>

  <h3>1. Baseline</h3>
  <p>
    We agree a set of buying-intent prompts — the questions a real buyer types
    when they are choosing, not researching. We run them across the major
    answer engines from clean sessions, and record what comes back: which
    brands are named, in what order, and which domains the answer cites.
  </p>

  <h3>2. Diagnosis</h3>
  <p>
    Absence has causes, and they are not all the same. A model may be unable to
    resolve your brand as an entity. It may be grounding the category on
    third-party sources you have no presence in. It may have a clear preference
    it will not be argued out of. The fix differs in each case.
  </p>

  <h3>3. Execution</h3>
  <p>
    Entity and structured-data work on your own properties, content built to be
    lifted into an answer, and placement into the third-party sources the
    models actually draw on. Most citations in AI answers come from earned
    media rather than brand-owned domains, so placement is core to the work
    rather than an add-on.
  </p>

  <h3>4. Re-measure</h3>
  <p>
    Against the same frozen prompt set, alongside a control set we deliberately
    leave untouched. Answer engines move on their own — models update,
    competitors act, indexes refresh. The control set is what separates our
    effect from theirs. Without it there is a correlation and no result.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pricing">Pricing</h2>

  <p>
    Three ways to engage. Scope is fixed in writing before anything starts.
  </p>

  <ul class="tiers">
    {
      tiers.map((tier) => (
        <li>
          <h3>{tier.name}</h3>
          <span class="price">
            {tier.price ?? 'On application'}
            {!tier.price && <span class="tbd">Rate card in preparation</span>}
          </span>
          <p>{tier.summary}</p>
          <ul>
            {tier.includes.map((item) => (
              <li>{item}</li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>

  <p class="note">
    Capacity is deliberately limited. Brandure takes a small number of
    engagements at a time so that each one gets the hours it needs.
  </p>

  <p><a href="/contact">Ask about an engagement</a></p>
</BaseLayout>
